1
00:00:00,261 --> 00:00:03,576
Every GPS satellite is launched
with its clock set wrong.

2
00:00:03,586 --> 00:00:04,761
On purpose.

3
00:00:04,996 --> 00:00:08,311
Your phone finds you by timing
radio signals from satellites

4
00:00:08,321 --> 00:00:10,321
twenty thousand kilometres up.

5
00:00:10,347 --> 00:00:13,768
Light covers thirty centimetres
in a billionth of a second.

6
00:00:13,778 --> 00:00:17,403
So a clock that's a billionth off
puts you thirty centimetres off.

7
00:00:17,539 --> 00:00:21,414
But Einstein showed that time doesn't
tick at the same rate everywhere.

8
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:25,886
Up there, gravity is weaker, so the
clock runs fast, by about forty-five

9
00:00:25,896 --> 00:00:27,496
microseconds a day.

10
00:00:27,630 --> 00:00:31,546
It's also moving at almost four
kilometres a second, which slows it down

11
00:00:31,556 --> 00:00:33,055
by about seven.

12
00:00:33,254 --> 00:00:36,018
Net result: thirty-eight
microseconds fast.

13
00:00:36,028 --> 00:00:37,554
Every single day.

14
00:00:38,753 --> 00:00:40,243
That sounds like nothing.

15
00:00:40,253 --> 00:00:43,453
But at the speed of light, it's
more than eleven kilometres.

16
00:00:43,510 --> 00:00:47,110
Ignore it, and your blue dot drifts
that far off in a single day.

17
00:00:47,510 --> 00:00:50,810
In 1977, not everyone believed it.

18
00:00:50,881 --> 00:00:54,571
So the Navy's test satellite,
NTS-2, flew with the fix built in,

19
00:00:54,581 --> 00:00:55,806
but switched off.

20
00:00:55,893 --> 00:00:59,193
They'd only turn it on if
Einstein turned out to be right.

21
00:01:00,012 --> 00:01:03,112
For about twenty days,
the clock ran uncorrected.

22
00:01:03,224 --> 00:01:06,124
Einstein's math predicted
how fast it would run.

23
00:01:06,182 --> 00:01:08,832
The clock matched him
to within one percent.

24
00:01:09,769 --> 00:01:11,244
They flipped the switch.

25
00:01:12,342 --> 00:01:16,442
Ever since, every GPS clock is
tuned a hair slow before launch.

26
00:01:16,513 --> 00:01:19,113
Wrong on the ground, so
it's right in the sky.

27
00:01:19,298 --> 00:01:23,573
And every time that blue dot finds
you, Einstein passes the test again.
